<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch01-points-vectors-space" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Points, Vectors, and Space</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>Coordinates turn points, displacements, and geometric shapes into objects we can calculate with. Starting from algebra and the Pythagorean theorem, we develop vectors, linear combinations, bases, distance, and equations of lines and planes. These supply the language used by the later calculus.</p>
  </introduction>

